  'tut-beat-tuks-varsity-football-final-2026-10-05',
  'TUT beat Tuks 3-2 to win a record fifth Varsity Football title',
  'Sport', '2026-10-05', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/sports-news/local-sports/2026/10/05/tut-beat-tuks-in-the-varsity-football-final-to-be-crowned-champions/',
  'Tshwane University of Technology came from behind to beat the University of Pretoria 3-2 in the Varsity Football final at Tuks Stadium.',
  'Tshwane University of Technology came from behind to beat the University of Pretoria 3-2 in the Varsity Football final at Tuks Stadium, giving TUT a record fifth title in the competition. Tuks took an early lead when Ntokozo Madela headed in a 17th-minute opener, but TUT levelled through Iviwe Sodidi''s second-half tap-in before Rearabilwe Mphahlele set up and then scored to put TUT ahead. Akani Rathokoa added a third goal late in the match to seal the win. Risen Albert, who had scored for Tuks, had to leave the field through injury.

It was only the second Varsity Football final contested between the two Pretoria rivals since the competition began in 2013. Tuks had gone into the match with one of the division''s strongest attacking and defensive records this season, but TUT''s experience at this stage of the competition proved decisive on the night.',
